{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0236","billNumberShort":"S.B. 236","billNumberLong":"SB0236S01","fileNumber":"2026FL1083","shortTitle":"Property Tax Exemption Process Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"GROVEK","primeSponsorName":"Sen. Grover, Keith","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"SHALLD","floorSponsorName":"Rep. Shallenberger, David","floorSponsorHouse":"H","generalProvisions":"This bill modifies provisions related to the property tax exemption process.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>establishes deadlines for:<hr><ltbullet1>a property owner to file an application with the county board of equalization for a property tax exemption; and<hr><ltbullet1>the county board of equalization to render a written decision on an application for a property tax exemption;<hr><ltbullet>authorizes the county board of equalization to request additional information from an applicant for a property tax exemption, in addition to or in lieu of holding a hearing on the application;<hr><ltbullet>provides for the county board of equalization to revoke a property tax exemption if property no longer qualifies for an exemption;<hr><ltbullet>requires the county board of equalization to include notice of a property owner's appeal rights in a written decision regarding a property tax exemption; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Gus Harb","fiscalAnalyst":"Jared Gibbs","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/23/2026","trackingID":"MGTWQXVPPN","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-02-02 11:22:30.400","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"descri